      "title": "Post-Polish (from Deno RTX3060 anime video)",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## MiniMax H3 Post-Polish\n\nFrom [s7JDBLfTGKI](https://youtu.be/s7JDBLfTGKI): generate H3 at workable res, then **sharpen/upscale + frame interpolate**.\n\n### Pipeline\n1. **LoadVideo** — put H3 MP4 into Comfy **input** (or pick from list)\n2. **GetVideoComponents** — split frames + original audio\n3. **Deno RTX VFX** — Deblur / VSR (optional; needs NVIDIA VFX install for Deno RTX nodes)\n4. **RIFE VFI ×2** — 24fps → **48fps** (smooth motion; true 60 needs non-integer mult or different tool)\n5. **CreateVideo + SaveVideo** — remux audio\n\n### If RTX VFX is not installed\n- Bypass / mute node 3 and wire GetVideoComponents.images → RIFE.frames directly\n- Or use MiniMax_LTX_Spatial_Full_Upscale.json for generative spatial upscale instead\n\n### Defaults for this 4090 box\n- Deblur Medium + scale 2.0 is a good starting point for 0.4–0.6 MP H3 clips\n- RIFE float16, multiplier 2, ensemble on\n\n### Companion generate graph\nMiniMax_H3_R2V_MultiRef_Deno.json (multi-image R2V)\n"
      ],
      "color": "#222",
      "bgcolor": "#000"
    },
